# Bookings API (task.md § contract)

Network layer **separate from UI** and **replaceable** with a real backend (UI talks only to `lib/api/bookings-client.ts`).

## Type

```typescript
type Booking = {
  id: string;
  date: string; // YYYY-MM-DD
  start: string; // HH:mm
  end: string; // HH:mm
  title?: string;
};
```

## Endpoints (exact paths from task)

- `GET /api/bookings?date=YYYY-MM-DD`
- `POST /api/bookings`
- `PATCH /api/bookings/:id`
- `DELETE /api/bookings/:id`

## Server (task.md)

- Validates **all business rules 1–7** via `lib/bookings/`
- Returns **409** on scheduling **conflict** (overlap), e.g. `{ error: "CONFLICT", message: "..." }`
- Other failures: 4xx/JSON `{ error, message }`; no stack traces to client

## Implementation layers

| Module                       | Role                                                                   |
| ---------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `lib/bookings/store.ts`      | In-memory persistence (MSW mock store OK elsewhere); resets on restart |
| Route Handlers               | HTTP ↔ validate ↔ store                                                |
| `lib/api/bookings-client.ts` | Typed fetch; map **409** to `BookingApiError` (or equivalent)          |

**Forbidden in UI:** direct `fetch('/api/bookings…')`.
